𐀁𐀵𐀛𐀍:
===Etymology===
{{unc|gmy}}. Perhaps a compound of {{m|grc|ἔτι|t=still, besides}} or {{m|grc|ἐτός|t=true}} and a derivative of the root of {{cog|grc|ὀνίνημι|t=to benefit}} (compare {{m|grc|ὄνια|t=useful things}} in Hesychius, and {{m|gmy|𐀃𐀙𐀵}}), with lengthening of the vowel at the start of the second member, hence roughly "special benefit". Compare the Cypriot syllabic ''pa-no-ni-o-ne'' (/panōnion/) on the Idalion bronze (ICS 217).<ref>{{cite-journal|author=Dijana Beljan|title=Doprinos interpretacijama mikenskih pločica: PY Eb 297 i PY Ep 704.5–6|trans-title=A Contribution to the Interpretation of Mycenaean Tablets PY Eb 297 and PY Ep 704.5–6|journal=Acta Illyrica|issue=5|year=2021|page=65|doi=10.54524/2490-3930.2021.63}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{head|gmy|noun|g=n|acc.|ts=etōnion}}

