𐀳𐀩𐀊𐀁:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|gmy|grk-pro||*teleiāmi}}, an athematic denominative verb derived from {{m|grk-pro||*teleiā}}, ultimately related to {{m|grk-pro||*télos}}, from {{der|gmy|ine-pro|*télh₂-os}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*telh₂-|t=to bear, undergo, endure}}.

Cognate with {{cog|grc|τέλος|t=service, obligation}} and {{cog|grc|τελείω|t=to perform, accomplish}}.<ref>Jiménez Delgado, José Miguel (2013), “[https://www.researchgate.net/publication/291100657_Mycenaean_te-re-ja Mycenaean ''te-re-ja'']”, ''Historische Sprachforschung'' 126, pp. 207–216.</ref><ref>Killen, John T.; Melena, José L., editors (2024), ''The New Documents in Mycenaean Greek'', Cambridge University Press, vol. 1, pp. 243–244; vol. 2, pp. 575–576, 1038.</ref>

===Verb===
