𐁆𐀐𐀥𐀪:
===Etymology===
The first element, {{lang|gmy|𐁆𐀐}} (''pʰuge-''), reflects the unaugmented root aorist seen in {{cog|grc|φεύγω|φύγε}} (“he escaped, fled”). The second element, {{lang|gmy|𐀥𐀪}} (''-gʷrīn-''), is connected with {{cog|grc|βρῖ}} (“heavily, mightily”) and the family of {{cog|grc|βριθύς}} (“heavy”) and {{cog|grc|βαρύς}} (“heavy”).

García Ramón interprets the compound as “he who escaped the heavy [one/thing]”, with the second member functioning as a transferred epithet. Suggested referents of “the heavy” include a [[spear]], [[misfortune]], an [[enemy]], or perhaps a [[stone]].

